{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788491774,"nonce":"eSVhJVJa+re2+mupHr2sBAI89kM=","title":"The map: a picture every turn, chosen by the mod, drawn the way the game draws it","message":"Part of the cockpit round, b4adee2. Design: RUNS/openrun-20260902/audit/COCKPIT.md\n§The screen (the map) and Appendix A. Feeds the screen spec's map panel and\nits guns gauge.\n\nWHAT\n\nThe screen's map panel: an ASCII crop of the home area plus margin, a second\ncrop around the stop's place when there is one, a PNG beside it that rwa\nrenders after every advance without being asked, and overlays that are the\ngame's own selection and placement drawings made into data.\n\nThe facts behind it. The run took seven pictures in 176 in-game days, all in\nthe first six hours, and none through the military build-out, the mech raids\nor the wipe. When it did look, it looked at a rectangle it chose after\ndeciding where to build, which is how it sealed its own workshop door. Its\nASCII map drew gravel, sand and rock as one character, and it wrote off 131\nfarmable gravel cells as sand. Nothing publishes turret range or line of sight\n(84 calls named a turret; \"every turret points outward at a gate … the lancer\nspent roughly 200,000 ticks unopposed inside the base\"). Nothing publishes a\nwind turbine's clearance or its output over time (four positions dry-run, two\nbuilt on nets disconnected from the base, both given up on). Both of those are\nthings the game draws for a player and neither is in any issue.\n\nSCOPE\n\n- map-dump gains overlay planes: turret range and line of sight per cell\n  (Building_TurretGun.DrawExtraSelectionOverlays; AttackVerb.verbProps.range;\n  GenSight.LineOfSight), wind-turbine clearance\n  (WindTurbineUtility.CalculateWindCells, drawn by PlaceWorker_WindTurbine),\n  power-net membership, roof, the home area, and gone-since-last (from the\n  provenance spec's destroyed rows). From those the mod computes the guns\n  gauge: guns covering each gate, and cells inside the walls covered by any gun.\n- one fixed ASCII alphabet, north up, with a legend printed under every crop,\n  that tells soil, gravel, sand, rock and ore apart. 855117a asks for ore\n  against rock and 8847053 is the orientation bug; both stay open as the\n  concrete items and this spec's alphabet is where they land.\n- the rectangle is the mod's: the home area's bounding box plus 8, capped at\n  80x60; over the cap, the bounding box of player buildings; over that, the\n  PNG only, and the screen says so. The agent can still ask map-dump for any\n  rectangle; that is the fetch, not the screen.\n- every placement dry run — build, place-layout, zone — replies with the ghost\n  the player sees before placing: the PlaceWorker DrawGhost cells and the\n  AllowsPlacing report, site-survey's crop (the ruling recorded on f7b6207\n  comment #7), the net a powered thing would join, and for a plant zone\n  whether the crop matures before the growing season ends (this run nearly\n  sowed 550 cells of rice on Fall 14).\n- `inspect {id}`: what the player's bottom pane says — GetInspectString and\n  GetInspectStringLowPriority (deterioration and why) — the thing's buttons\n  from GetGizmos with label, type, state and disabledReason (the read half of\n  9717e52; the press half stays there), and the thing's overlay.\n- rwa renders frames/\u003ctick\u003e.png after every advance. The render exists\n  (f7b6207); what was never built is calling it unasked.\n\nACCEPTANCE\n\n- On a bench with a turret and a wind turbine: the screen's map draws the ring\n  and the clearance; `inspect` on the turbine names the wall when one is placed\n  in its clearance; the guns gauge's coverage changes when the turret is\n  destroyed.\n- A dry-run build of a wind turbine over a tree reports the tree; ten tiles\n  from the grid it reports that it would join no net.\n- Gravel, sand and rock print as three different characters; row 0 is north\n  and the ruler says so; the legend is under every crop.\n- After each advance in a run, frames/\u003ctick\u003e.png exists and matches a\n  re-render of the saved dump byte for byte.\n- A fresh reader shown only the PNG answers room count, door locations and\n  which room holds the stove — f7b6207's acceptance, still owed, discharged\n  here or there.\n- Whether the agent OPENS the picture is UNKNOWN and is measured, not assumed:\n  the first run on the cockpit counts Read calls on frames/*.png in the harness\n  log and reports the number.\n\nABSORBS\n\nThe read half of 9717e52. f7b6207 stays open under this spec for its\nlegibility read; 8847053 and 855117a stay open as the concrete items.","files":null}]}